      "data": {
        "text": "**Planning File Creation**\n\nOkay, I'm generating the new Python files for the NoSQL integration, excluding `upsert_document.py`. I have a clear focus on the nine new files, paying special attention to how each \"scored\" file needs to leverage a distinct external provider. This structure is intended to cover the specific requirements.\n\n\n**Defining File Structure**\n\nI've examined `upsert_document.py` for database interaction patterns, informing `database_client.py` and `database_models.py`. DynamoDB is selected for `fetch_document.py`, `query_documents.py`, and `conditional_update.py`. Now, I'm integrating Google Cloud services for LATER-STEP files, using Generative AI for `record_summary.py`, Vertex AI Safety for `record_text_safety.py`, and the Translation API for `record_translate.py`. Amazon S3 will handle `record_export_archive.py`. I'll start with implementing the DynamoDB client in `database_client.py`.\n\n\n**Outlining the Implementation**\n\nI've got a detailed implementation plan now. I'll begin by examining `upsert_document.py` to establish a foundation for `database_client.py` and `database_models.py`. I'm starting the DynamoDB-based files, and am ready to start on `fetch_document.py`. I've chosen Google Cloud Generative AI for summarization, Vertex AI Safety for content moderation, and the Translation API for translation, and Amazon S3 for archival. I'm prioritizing the DynamoDB client implementation in `database_client.py`.\n\n\n",
