      "data": {
        "text": "**Analyzing Conditional Updates**\n\nI've been examining how to approach \"conditional updates\" in Azure Cosmos DB, since there isn't a direct equivalent to DynamoDB's `ConditionExpression`. I am now focusing on the implications of using `If-Match` headers for concurrency control, as an alternative to implementing stored procedures for more complex scenarios.\n\n\n**Refining Conditional Upserts**\n\nI'm now implementing the approach within `conditional_update.py`. The \"conditional update\" concept in Azure Cosmos DB relies on reading, modifying, and upserting with `If-Match` headers for concurrency control, an alternative to stored procedures. I'm demonstrating an upsert after fetching, assuming application logic handles the condition, while utilizing the `_etag` for conditional update with `upsert_item`.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789891110010,
          "start": 1789891107277
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bdd2d9cd001Je6Trjh41dfHs1",
